; with `calc on`, a part of a rule is computed as soon as its variables have values: matching
; `3! = 3 * 2!` against "factorial-step" (`$n! = $n * ($n - 1)!`) computes `3 - 1` to `2`
load numbers
calc on

3 > 0
3! = 3 * 2!                     ; by factorial-step
2 > 0
2! = 2 * 1!
expect "ProofError"
    2! = 2 * 0!                 ; `2 - 1` is not `0`

; and a definition works with numbers directly
arity f 1
def f($x) = $x * $x
f(3) = 9
f(2) = 4
expect "ProofError"
    f(3) = 6
